        "original_id": "4fe9dda8-1c26-5a90-b65e-4b392c56b232",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Frank Tashlin, Craig Serling\n- Works: Brother Brat, Jam\n- Companies: Warner Bros., Looney Tunes\n- Roles: animator, screenwriter, film director, film producer, television editor\n- Awards: Primetime Emmy nominations\n\nFacts:\n- Frank Tashlin, born Francis Fredrick von Taschlein on February 19, 1913, was an American animator, screenwriter, and film director.\n- Brother Brat was released in 1944 as a Warner Bros. Looney Tunes theatrical cartoon short starring Porky Pig and directed by Frank Tashlin.\n- Frank Tashlin died on May 5, 1972.\n- Craig Serling is an American film director, film producer, screenwriter, and television editor.\n- Craig Serling received multiple Primetime Emmy nominations for Outstanding Picture Editing for Non-Fiction Programming.\n- Craig Serling made his feature directorial debut in 2006 with the film Jam.",
